public/pi_board.wasm
# public/unicorn.js is committed: it is a prebuilt patched fork artifact that the
# CI build cannot regenerate (the fork source lives only in /tmp/opencode on the
# dev machine). build.sh falls back to this committed copy when the local fork
# build dir is absent.
# qemu-wasm Linux-boot artifacts.
# The ENGINE (out.js / .wasm / .worker.js) is COMMITTED: it is our rebuilt
# pthread/MTTCG engine with the pi3-ctl N4 bridge (regenerated by
# scripts/build-linux.sh, not by CI). The .data is now a ~38 MB INITRAMFS
# image (dtb + kernel + gzipped-cpio rootfs loaded via -initrd) and load.js
# (preload packager, must match .data) is committed too, so the Pages deploy is
# self-contained and uses the fast initramfs boot path (no SD/MMC emulation).
# To regenerate the image locally, re-run the initramfs build (module.js uses
# -initrd) and keep load.js offsets in sync.
# public/linux/qemu-system-aarch64.data  (COMMITTED)
# public/linux/load.js                   (COMMITTED)
# From-source qemu-wasm build output (single-thread; NOT the live engine)
public/linux-fromsrc/
# qemu-wasm source clone + build scratch (ephemeral; do not commit)
scripts/.build/